hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"42","Subḥāna Rabbiyal-`Aẓīm. ¤ ---------------------------------¤ [three times] Glory to my Lord the Exalted (three times in Arabic)"
"43","Subḥānaka Allāhumma Rabbanā wa biḥamdika Allāhum-maghfir lī. ¤ ---------------------------------¤ Glory is to You , O Allah , our Lord , and praise is Yours . O Allah , forgive me."
"44","Subbūḥun, Quddūsun, Rabbul-malā'ikati warrūḥ. ¤--------------------------------- ¤ Glory (to You) , Most Holy (are You) , Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"45","Allāhumma laka raka`tu, wa bika 'āmantu, wa laka 'aslamtu khasha`a laka sam`ee wa baṣarī, wa mukhkhī, wa `aẓmī, wa `aṣabī, wa mastaqalla bihi qadamī. ¤ ---------------------------------¤ O Allah , to You I bow (in prayer) and in You I believe and to You I have submitted. Before You my hearing is humbled, and my sight, and my mind, my bones, my nerves and what my feet have mounted upon (for travel)."
"46","Subḥāna dhil-jabarūti, walmalakūti, walkibriyā'i, wal`aẓamati. ¤ ---------------------------------¤ Glory is to You, Master of power, of dominion, of majesty and greatness."
